   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualifications for\nholding the offices of city controller and city engineer in the city of\nAmsterdam",
    "basePrintNo": "S6662",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6662-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6662\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualifications\nfor holding the offices of city controller and city engineer in the city\nof Amsterdam\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation will allow the City of Amsterdam to hire an individual\nresiding outside of the City of Amsterdam for the positions of city\ncontroller and city engineer, provided that the individual resides in\nMontgomery County or an adjoining county within the State of New York.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 3 of the public officers law is amended by adding a new subdivi-\nsion 73 which allows an individual residing outside of the City of Amst-\nerdam, either within Montgomery County or an adjoining county, to hold\nthe office of city controller or city engineer.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation will increase the pool of candidates eligible to hold\nthe offices of City Controller and City Engineer.  The Amsterdam Common\nCouncil and Mayor of Amsterdam have submitted a home rule request.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
